                                                "text": "Holonyms: calendar year; year"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6c68ecf-917d-4591-a14e-24fb37c1ba4b",
                                                "sense_id": "95552511-66c2-3907-a48c-8f690666fcc4",
                                                "text": "By October it was advancing steadily toward Pangwa, encountering meager resistance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3abd8f0f-9304-345e-b980-444cc132e3c2",
                                        "entry_id": "9efb1714-d3e2-3d89-b7c6-44c1000c2a54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female given name transferred from the month name."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f969f9dd-5847-441f-b4d7-ba9ca7b99d82",
                                                "sense_id": "3abd8f0f-9304-345e-b980-444cc132e3c2",
                                                "text": "The other one [book] I just read is October Suite by Maxine Clair (Random House, $23.95). It's about a woman named October. She's a young black schoolteacher in the 1950s ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4954636-01c1-4cfa-a53f-5ba26f8323b7",
                                                "sense_id": "3abd8f0f-9304-345e-b980-444cc132e3c2",
                                                "text": "From somewhere in the distance came the screaming whine of an emergency vehicle's siren. Lance flipped open his phone. “Get me the address of a woman named October Guinness . . . That's right, October,” he said again, [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "October",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ad7c447-1285-3bd5-8f7f-da569c87717e",
                                        "entry_id": "1d5d8442-8011-32c6-a4bf-be58fb1e3e5c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of ale traditionally brewed in October."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "604c4c21-26f3-4586-a96d-31e1845b09b1",
                                                "sense_id": "2ad7c447-1285-3bd5-8f7f-da569c87717e",
                                                "text": "Sir, if I vvas vvorthy to adviſe you, I vvou'd have a Bottle of good October by me. Shall I ſet a Cup of old Stingo at your Elbovv?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e3c6c4d-37d4-4e90-b8f0-e8bcac593a1a",
                                                "sense_id": "2ad7c447-1285-3bd5-8f7f-da569c87717e",
                                                "text": "[T]he gate of a large chateau, of a most noble and venerable appearance […] induced them to alight and view the apartments, contrary to their first intention of drinking a glass of his October at the door."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c426538-fd5b-46ab-9f76-4ad1fce8f17f",
                                                "sense_id": "2ad7c447-1285-3bd5-8f7f-da569c87717e",
                                                "text": "Sir George, borne along in his chair, peered up at this well-known window--well-known, since in the Oxford of 1767 a man's rooms were furnished if he had tables and chairs, store of beef and October, an apple-pie and Common Room port—and seeing the casement brilliantly lighted, smiled a trifle contemptuously."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "October",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
